  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As far as I can tell this only affects one particular avatar, and only when using --legacy-fbt-calibrate.\nThe first calibration after startup goes just fine, but the second one onward causes the avatar to float, so you need to playspace move to calibrate well. Toggling avatar measurement works around the issue, but subsequent calibrations with the avatar still cause it to float.\nDoing reset avatar does not seem to help.\nThe problem does not manifest when using legacy IK.\nThere is a public sample of the avatar that also exhibits the same symptom, uploaded by its author at avatar ID: https://vrchat.com/home/avatar/avtr_9009b6ee-c483-4144-9e93-81b93803f11c\nIt is SDK2, so testing whether reset avatar does something is not possible, however.\nHere is a video of me explaining the problem:\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/946881839400882196/979233061797523456/2022-05-26_05-58-33.mp4\nHere is me showing absence (or at least not being able to detect) this bug when using non-legacy calibrate:\nhttps://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/946881839400882196/979234879965392936/2022-05-26_06-08-16.mp4",
